# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it.
# `.env` holds APP_SECRET and the SMTP password — it must never be copied into
# a layer, which is why the runtime reads its configuration from the
# environment instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo

.git
.github
.claude
.dual-graph

*.md
!README.md
docs
schemas

# The agent binaries `/install.sh` hands out live in `clients/agent/bin`, which
# CI populates. They are deliberately not in the image: shipping cross-compiled
# binaries would double its size, and `routes/download.ts` already answers with
# a clear "build it or take one from the releases" when they are absent.
clients

**/*.test.ts
**/*.integration.test.ts
